-- The laws that follow from Ord's (core/models.strata, `OrdLaws`), proven
-- once here from `irreflexive` and `transitive`. Each is a fact in every
-- proof bounded by `Ord` (simplify uses it), never a hypothesis or an
-- obligation of an `impl`.

theorem ord.asymmetric[A: Ord](a: A, b: A): a < b ==> !(b < a) := by
  intro h1 h2
  apply irreflexive(a)
  exact transitive(a, b, a)(h1)(h2)
